    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/3325-Patrick-F-Taylor-Hall/Assistant--Associate--or-Full-Professor-of-Research_R00119770": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Research",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-13\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Research     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Engineering - School of Electrical and Computer Engineering (Shuangqing Wei (00007502))     Work Location: 3325 Patrick F. Taylor Hall     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Assistant Professor of Research 40% Sponsored Research: Conduct innovative research in data-driven modeling, communications, networking, machine learning, distributed optimization, and intelligent autonomous systems for distributed maritime operations involving both surface and underwater autonomous vehicles. Design and develop mathematical models, algorithms, engineering simulations, software tools, experiments, and testing methodologies for distributed multi-agent systems, resilient communications, intelligent sensing, autonomous decision-making, and cooperative autonomous operations. Manage, oversee, and design engineering simulations, experiments, and tests, and collect and analyze data while ensuring data integrity, quality control, and research reproducibility. Maintain currency with relevant state-of-the-art technologies, equipment, systems, communications and networking methods, and machine learning techniques. Publish research findings in leading peer-reviewed journals and conferences. Work under the general direction of senior investigators while demonstrating increasing independence in research design and execution. 35% Supervise Graduate Students and Postdoctoral Researchers: Provide research supervision and technical mentoring to graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, research associates, and other research personnel. Guide research planning, technical development, experimental and simulation activities, publication preparation, sponsor deliverables, and professional development while fostering a collaborative and inclusive research environment. Provide day-to-day technical guidance to students and postdoctoral researchers in coordination with project principal investigators. 25% Research Program Development and External Funding: Identify funding opportunities and participate in developing competitive research proposals for federal agencies, industry, and other sponsors. Initiate and develop contacts and collaborations with grant and contract agencies, faculty members, industry partners, and other academic institutions to support the growth of externally funded research programs. Contribute to proposal preparation, technical planning, budgeting, project reporting, sponsor communications, and the preparation of technical reports and other research-related documentation. Contribute technical ideas, preliminary results, and written materials to collaborative proposal development. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline. Specific Experience: Demonstrated research accomplishments through peer-reviewed publications. Evidence of the ability and potential to conduct high-quality independent and collaborative research. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline. Specific Experience: Postdoctoral or industrial research experience. Experience participating in federally sponsored research. Experience mentoring graduate or undergraduate researchers. Experience contributing to research proposal development. Associate Professor of Research 40% Sponsored Research: Conduct innovative research in data-driven modeling, communications, networking, machine learning, distributed optimization, and intelligent autonomous systems for distributed maritime operations involving both surface and underwater autonomous vehicles. Design and develop mathematical models, algorithms, engineering simulations, software tools, experiments, and testing methodologies for distributed multi-agent systems, resilient communications, intelligent sensing, autonomous decision-making, and cooperative autonomous operations. Manage, oversee, and design engineering simulations, experiments, and tests, and collect and analyze data while ensuring data integrity, control, and research reproducibility. Maintain currency with relevant state-of-the-art technologies, equipment, systems, communications and networking methods, and machine learning techniques. Publish research findings in leading peer-reviewed journals and conferences. Lead substantial research tasks or projects and coordinate technical activities across multidisciplinary teams. 35% Supervise Graduate Students and Postdoctoral Researchers: Provide research supervision and technical mentoring to graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, research associates, and other research personnel. Guide research planning, technical development, experimental and simulation activities, publication preparation, sponsor deliverables, and professional development while fostering a collaborative and inclusive research environment. Supervise graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, and research personnel, and mentor junior researchers in scholarly publication and professional development. 25% Research Program Development and External Funding: Identify funding opportunities and participate in developing competitive research proposals for federal agencies, industry, and other sponsors. Initiate and develop contacts and collaborations with grant and contract agencies, faculty members, industry partners, and other academic institutions to support the growth of externally funded research programs. Contribute to proposal preparation, technical planning, budgeting, project reporting, sponsor communications, and the preparation of technical reports and other research-related documentation. Develop and lead proposal sections or complete proposals and serve, as appropriate, as Principal Investigator, Co-Principle Investigator, or key personnel on externally funded projects. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline with 5 years of post Ph.D. research experience. Specific Experience: Strong and sustained record of peer-reviewed publications demonstrating research excellence. Demonstrated success in obtaining or making significant contributions to externally funded research. Experience supervising graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, or research personnel. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline with 5 years of post Ph.D. research experience. Specific Experience: Experience serving as Principal Investigator, Co-Principal Investigator, or key personnel on externally funded research. Experience leading multidisciplinary research projects. Established national reputation in one or more relevant research areas. Experience managing project schedules, milestones, personnel, and sponsor deliverables. Professor of Research 40% Sponsored Research: Conduct innovative research in data-driven modeling, communications, networking, machine learning, distributed optimization, and intelligent autonomous systems for distributed maritime operations involving both surface and underwater autonomous vehicles. Design and develop mathematical models, algorithms, engineering simulations, software tools, experiments, and testing methodologies for distributed multi-agent systems, resilient communications, intelligent sensing, autonomous decision-making, and cooperative autonomous operations. Manage, oversee, and design engineering simulations, experiments, and tests, and collect and analyze data while ensuring data integrity, control, and research reproducibility. Maintain currency with relevant state-of-the-art technologies, equipment, systems, communications and networking methods, and machine learning techniques. Publish research findings in leading peer-reviewed journals and conferences. Provide senior scientific and technical leadership for major sponsored research activities and coordinate research across multiple investigators, disciplines, and partner organizations. 35% Supervise Graduate Students and Postdoctoral Researchers: Provide research supervision and technical mentoring to graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, research associates, and other research personnel. Guide research planning, technical development, experimental and simulation activities, publication preparation, sponsor deliverables, and professional development while fostering a collaborative and inclusive research environment. Lead and mentor multidisciplinary teams of graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, research faculty, research associates, and technical staff. 25% Research Program Development and External Funding: Identify funding opportunities and participate in developing competitive research proposals for federal agencies, industry, and other sponsors. Initiate and develop contacts and collaborations with grant and contract agencies, faculty members, industry partners, and other academic institutions to support the growth of externally funded research programs. Contribute to proposal preparation, technical planning, budgeting, project reporting, sponsor communications, and the preparation of technical reports and other research-related documentation. Lead the development of major multidisciplinary proposals, cultivate sponsor and industry relationships, and provide management leadership for research portfolios, budgets, schedules, deliverables, personnel, and sponsor reporting. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline with 10 years of post Ph.D. research experience. Specific Experience: Internationally recognized record of scholarly achievement and high-impact peer-reviewed publications. Sustained record of externally funded research as Principal Investigator, Co-Principal Investigator, or equivalent research leader. Demonstrated experience leading multidisciplinary research programs and managing sponsored research projects. Proven record of mentoring graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, and research personnel. Demonstrated record of project management and proposal development. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline with 10 years of post Ph.D. research experience. Specific Experience: Experience leading large multidisciplinary research initiatives involving universities, industry, and government agencies. Experience developing long-term research partnerships and strategic sponsored research programs. Professional leadership through editorial service, conference organization, or leadership roles in professional societies. Record of technology transition, patents, software dissemination, or other research impact.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: The Division of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) in the School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science (EECS) at Louisiana State University invites applications for a non-tenure-track Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Research position. The successful candidate will conduct innovative sponsored research in data-driven modeling, communications, networking, artificial intelligence, machine learning, intelligent autonomous systems, and distributed maritime operations involving both surface and underwater autonomous vehicles. The successful candidate will join a vibrant and collaborative interdisciplinary research team consisting of faculty, research scientists, postdoctoral researchers, and graduate students from Electrical and Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Mechanical Engineering, and Mathematics. The team conducts cutting-edge research, supported by federal agencies and industry partners, in distributed multi-agent systems, autonomous maritime operations, communications, networking, machine learning, and intelligent autonomous systems. The successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate across disciplines, contribute to large multidisciplinary research projects, and help develop innovative technologies with real-world applications. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to the growth of externally funded research programs through high-quality research, scholarly publications, mentoring of graduate students and postdocs, and the development of competitive research proposals. Questions regarding this position can be directed to Shuangqing Wei at swei@lsu.edu. Due to sponsor requirements associated with federally funded research, applicants must be U.S. citizens or lawful permanent residents (Green Card holders). Applications from individuals who do not meet this requirement will not be considered.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 13, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): February 23, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/L0100-Hebert-Law-Center/Collection-Services-Librarian_R00121210": {
      "title": "Collection Services Librarian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-13\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Collection Services Librarian     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Law - LLIS - Resource Management (Amanda Arceneaux (00004773))     Work Location: L0100 Hebert Law Center     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Job Summary: The LSU Paul M. Hebert Law Center seeks a Collection Services Librarian . Reporting to the Head of Resource Management, the Collection Services Librarian is responsible for developing, assessing, acquiring, and providing access to the Law Library's print and electronic collections in support of the teaching, research, and service missions of the Law Center. The position coordinates collection development activities, acquisitions workflows, serials management, cataloging, and metadata services to ensure that library resources are discoverable and accessible to users. They must be able to function in a collegial, teamwork-oriented environment with a strong service orientation; be self-motivated, with excellent attention to detail and superior organizational and analytical skills; maintain strong communication and interpersonal skills, and have the ability to communicate clearly, effectively, and professionally, and in a timely manner; capacity to work independently and as a collaborative team member. Candidates holding a J.D. in addition to the required M.L.S. may participate in legal research instruction and other faculty responsibilities as assigned. Job Responsibilities: Lead collection development activities for the Law Library, including evaluating and assessing existing collections, identifying collection strengths and gaps, recommending purchases and cancellations, and working collaboratively with reference librarians and faculty to select resources that support curricular and research needs. Participate in collection assessment, inventory, preservation, and deselection projects as appropriate. (25%) Manage acquisitions workflows for print and electronic resources, including ordering library materials through GOBI and other vendors, receiving materials, maintaining standing orders and subscriptions, monitoring expenditures, and communicating with publishers, vendors, and consortia regarding acquisitions and collection needs. (25%) Perform copy cataloging for both firm and continuing materials in all formats, following MARC metadata standards, RDA, LC Subject Headings, and LC Classification practices; ensure metadata quality and consistency to support discovery and access. Familiarity with OCLC Connexion and integrated library systems is desired. (25%) Engage in ongoing professional development to remain current with emerging trends, standards, and best practices in collection development, acquisitions, cataloging, metadata, and legal information services. Actively participate in local, state, and national library and law library organizations and associations. (10%) Collaborate with library faculty and staff to develop policies, workflows, and procedures related to collection development, acquisitions, metadata management, and resource access. Participate in library planning, special projects, and initiatives that support the strategic goals of the Law Library. (10%) Perform additional duties as assigned in support of the library’s mission and evolving needs. ( 5%)   Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in Library and Information Science (MLIS, MLS, or equivalent) from an ALA-accredited institution. 3 years of professional experience in an academic, law, or research library involving acquisitions, collection development, cataloging, metadata, or technical services. Knowledge of current cataloging standards, including MARC 21, RDA, and authority control practices. Experience working with integrated library systems and bibliographic utilities such as OCLC. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects and workflows effectively. Excellent organizational, analytical, interpersonal, and communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a collegial environment. Preferred Qualifications: 5 years experience in a law library or other academic library. Knowledge of legal publishing and legal information resources. Experience with collection assessment and collection development planning. Experience with Exlibris’ Alma: Acquisitions, Resources, Analytics, Metadata Editor; familiarity with vendor platforms such a GOBI. Experience managing serials and continuing resources. J.D. from an ABA-accredited law school. Teaching, training, or instructional experience.      Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Interested candidates are asked to submit a cover letter, CV/Resume, and (3) three letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For additional information about this position or the associated salary range, please contact Amanda Arceneaux at Amanda.Arceneaux@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 13, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): April 3, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/3079-Energy-Coast-and-Environment-Building/Director-and-State-Geologist_R00121458": {
      "title": "Director and State Geologist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-13\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Director and State Geologist     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM ORED - Energy Institute (John C Flake (00002004))     Work Location: 3079 Energy, Coast, and Environment Building     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: The LSU Energy Institute is seeking applications for the position of Director of the Louisiana Geological Survey (LGS). The Louisiana Geological Survey is the official geological survey of the State of Louisiana and is housed within the LSU Energy Institute pursuant to Louisiana R.S. 17:1492.The Director serves as Louisiana's State Geologist and provides strategic leadership and overall management of the Louisiana Geological Survey. In this capacity, the Director serves as the chief scientific authority for the Survey while overseeing statewide geological investigations, mapping activities, subsurface studies, geological hazard assessments, geological data resources, field operations, core and sample repositories, and related scientific and technical initiatives. The Director works collaboratively with state agencies, academic researchers, industry stakeholders, policymakers, and external partners to advance the Survey's mission, scientific excellence, and long-term development. A faculty appointment at Louisiana State University may also be considered, consistent with qualifications and university policies. Job Responsibilities: Provide strategic leadership and overall management of the Louisiana Geological Survey while serving as Louisiana's State Geologist. Direct the Survey's scientific, technical, administrative, and operational activities. Provide scientific leadership and technical direction for statewide geological investigations, mapping activities, subsurface studies, geological hazard assessments, and related research initiatives. Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with government agencies, academic institutions, industry partners, and other stakeholders, and pursue external funding opportunities through grants, contracts, and strategic partnerships to support and expand the Survey's mission. (35%) Pursuant to Louisiana R.S. 17:1492, oversee the maintenance of current surface and subsurface geological surveys of the State of Louisiana. In addition, oversee the stewardship of the LGS core facility to ensure that cores, logs, and data are preserved, inventoried, and easily accessed by internal and external stakeholders. (25%) Serve as the primary spokesperson and subject matter expert for the Louisiana Geological Survey. Represent the Survey before policymakers, governmental entities, industry stakeholders, academic audiences, professional organizations, media, and the public through presentations, testimony, technical briefings, outreach activities, and other engagement efforts. Communicate complex geological information in a manner that supports informed decision-making and public understanding. (25%) Contribute to Louisiana Geological Survey and LSU Energy Institute activities, including conferences, workshops, and meetings, and collaborate across LSU academic departments and colleges on geology, energy, and other interdisciplinary initiatives. (10%) Other duties as assigned. (5%) Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in geology or related field and 7 years of experience. Eligible for Louisiana Professional Geoscientist licensure. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply--a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D in geology or related field. A record appropriate for senior rank at LSU; demonstrated scientific leadership; eligibility for Louisiana Professional Geoscientist licensure; and strong communication skills. The candidate should be familiar with coastal geology, deltaic systems, Class VI and or groundwater regulations, state surveys, and federal or regulatory policies.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and three (3) professional references including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address. Please attach ALL required documents under the \"Resume/CV\" section of your application. A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if available). However, original transcripts are required before hiring (if applicable). Due to the nature of the position and/or position responsibilities, this position shall be subject to pre-employment screenings in accordance with University Policy as required and RS:17 screenings (https://www.legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?p=y&d=1297548). For questions or concerns about updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Dr. John Flake at johnflake@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 13, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): February 10, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): N     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/2200-BEC-South-Grad-Pavilion/Instructor_R00121454": {
      "title": "Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-13\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Instructor     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM COB - Stephenson Department of Entrepreneurship and Information Systems (Edward Fisk Watson III (00001317))     Work Location: 2200 BEC South Grad Pavilion     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Job Summary: This instructor position will be a joint appointment teaching courses for the Stephenson Department of Entrepreneurship and Information Systems, as well as, the Rucks Department of Management. Normal teaching load is four courses or sections per semester, i.e., eight courses or sections per calendar year. While the specific courses may vary, it is anticipated that 6 of the courses will be Entrepreneurship courses and 2 will be Management courses. Job Responsibilities: 90% - Teaching courses for the Stephenson Department of Entrepreneurship and Information Systems, as well as, the Rucks Department of Management. Normal teaching load is four courses or sections per semester, i.e., eight courses or sections per calendar year. 10% - Provide service to the department(s) and College. Minimum Qualifications: Education level: Master's in Entrepreneurship, Management, Business Administration, or related field Years of Experience: 0-3 years Specific Experience: Teaching or professional experience in entrepreneurship or management Preferred Qualifications: Years of Experience: 3-5 years Specific Experience: Teaching entrpreneurship or management courses in a business school Competencies: Teaching - Proficient Effective Communication Skills - Advanced Teamwork and collaboration - Advanced     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please attach a Resume/CV. A copy of the transcript may be attached, but an original transcript will be required prior to hire. For questions about this position or it's associated salary range, please reach out to Dr. Ed Watson, ewatson@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 13, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): April 11, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
