    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/0402-Julian-T-White-Hall/Director-of-the-School-of-Interior-Design_R00121411": {
      "title": "Director of the School of Interior Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Director of the School of Interior Design     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM College of Art and Design (Arne R. Flaten (00280418))     Work Location: 0402 Julian T. White Hall     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Applications and nominations are invited for the position of Director, School of Interior Design, Louisiana State University.  The appointment will commence July 1, 2027.  The School seeks a dynamic colleague to contribute to the teaching, research, and service missions of the School, the interdisciplinary setting of the College of Art and Design, and the collaborative opportunities of Louisiana State University.  The Director is the executive officer of the School and is responsible to the President and Chancellor through the Dean of the College of Art and Design and the Academic Affairs Executive Vice President and Provost.  The Director of the School of Interior Design is expected to provide dynamic visionary leadership and exhibit dedication to advancement in all areas of the School in alignment with the mission and goals of the College and University. The Director is responsible for student and faculty involvement in study and research that promote leadership, global engagement, interdisciplinary collaboration, innovation, and culturally competency.   Louisiana provides distinct educational and research opportunities to students and faculty.  At Louisiana State University we are uniquely positioned to address economic development, the coast and environment, culture and the arts, and health and well-being within the Mississippi River Delta and larger global community.  The School of Interior Design is housed within the College of Art and Design along with the School of Architecture, the School of Art, and the Robert Reich School of Landscape Architecture. The School awards the Bachelor of Interior Design degree and the Master of Science in Interior Design (MSID), both of which are accredited by the Council for Interior Design Accreditation (CIDA).  The College also has a Doctor of Design Program (DDes) for continued study and research.  The College’s Fabrication Factory is equipped with laser cutters, CNC routers, plasma cutters and 3D printers, which are available for student projects and faculty research.   The Director: provides leadership for the educational programs, budgeting, and focus of the School; assumes responsibility for the management of quality, effectiveness and progress of the School; promotes the public image of the School and University; provides professional leadership and increases Interior Design visibility; encourages good public relations and promotes excellence in teaching and scholarship; encourages and facilitates good teaching research; enforces standards, orients new faculty members, and facilitates faculty growth and development.   The Director will participate on College and School committees as assigned; conduct research and scholarly work; perform service to the University and community. The Director may also teach undergraduate or graduate courses as deemed suitable based on her/his background and the School’s needs.     Minimum Qualifications: Master’s Degree in Interior Design or related field Distinguished record in teaching, research, and service sufficient to merit tenure. Hold a NCIDQ certificate or equivalent licensure abroad or in related field Distinguished record of scholarly, and/or professional practice in Interior Design Ability to demonstrate academic administrative experience including development, personnel, student recruitment, and budget management.   Preferred Qualifications: A record of successful leadership, collaboration in practice, research, and administrative experience is desired. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Application review will begin December 1, 2026, and will continue until a candidate is selected.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Applicants should provide the following through the university’s online application portal: 1. Letter of interest 2. Current resume 3. Names and contact information of three professional references 4. Portfolio (pdf or link) of professional and/or academic work Questions should be directed to the following: Elizabeth Duffy, Assistant Dean of Finance and Administration eduffy@lsu.edu     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 9, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): April 7, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/0151C-Charles-E-Coates-Hall/Assistant-Professor---Performance-Studies_R00121408": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Performance Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor - Performance Studies     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM HSS - Communication Studies (Bryan McCann (00007537))     Work Location: 0151C Charles E. Coates Hall     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Department of Communication Studies seeks a scholar-artist for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position, beginning August 2027. We are looking for an innovative maker and theorist to conduct high-quality research—both written and staged—teach undergraduate and graduate courses, and actively mentor students in original arts-based scholarship. As our department is dedicated to the ongoing evolution and methodological growth of the field of performance studies, we seek candidates actively engaged in arts-based research who will make substantive use of our experimental performance laboratory, the HopKins Black Box theatre. The successful candidate will view performance not merely as an object of study, but as a primary methodology and way of knowing. We welcome interpretations of \"performance studies\" and strongly encourage applications from scholars whose backgrounds may bridge Communication Studies, Theatre, and Interdisciplinary Arts, provided they are committed to experimental, research-driven performance, and to utilizing their hands-on performance experience to drive rigorous academic publication and create original performances in the HopKins Black Box theatre. Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. in Performance Studies, Communication, Theatre, or a closely related discipline (by the time of appointment). A demonstrated, active agenda of arts-based research and creative practice. Research credentials commensurate with a Comprehensive Doctoral University. Evidence of excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications We seek a performance scholar-practitioner with a strong publication and production record (or clear potential) whose work complements existing faculty strengths. The ideal candidate will have experience and a deep commitment to working within a performance laboratory setting and mentoring students in original, devised, or experimental performance making. We are particularly interested in applicants utilizing practice-as-research and arts-based methodologies. Areas of topical interest are open, but we especially welcome candidates whose work bridges critical performance studies with theatrical practice, which may include: Devised, experimental, and ensemble-based theatre Applied theatre, community engagement, and social practice Experimental directing and dramaturgy Live art, intermediality, and multimedia performance Site-specific performance, spatial practices, and public memory Digital, algorithmic, and virtual performance spaces The performance of identity, embodiment, and power (including intersectional, queer, or decolonial frameworks) Salary Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Application Timeline Application review will begin November 12, 2026. The position will remain open until filled.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Before uploading, applicants should assemble all documents into one PDF file in the following order: 1. Cover Letter: Addressing your experience and dedication to both written research and arts-based creative practice, teaching, and service. 2. Curriculum Vitae. 3. Description of Research Program: (Limit to 2 pages). Please explicitly address how you envision utilizing the HopKins Black Box theatre for your original performance works. 4. Sample of Scholarly Writing. 5. Portfolio of Creative Scholarship: Evidence of arts-based research, performance practice, or theatrical creation (e.g., links to video samples, prompt books, production photos, or critical reviews). 6. Evidence of Teaching Excellence: (Limit to 2 pages). 7. References: A list of the names, titles, addresses, and contact information for three references who may be asked to provide letters of recommendation after the initial review. 8. Job Specification: The Department of Communication Studies is hiring for two assistant professors of performance studies this year; this position is 100% housed in Communication Studies. Any candidates wishing to be considered for both positions must apply to each position independently and should indicate in writing that they are willing to be considered for both positions. Applicants may also attach copies of transcripts to their applications; original transcripts are required prior to hire. Please contact the chair of the search committee, Dr. Travis Brisini (tbrisini@lsu.edu) with questions regarding the status of your application or salary ranges.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 9, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): April 7, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/0331-AR-Choppin-Hall---Chemistry/Assistant-Professor-in-Computational-Chemistry--Broadly-Defined-_R00120415": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Computational Chemistry (Broadly Defined)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor in Computational Chemistry (Broadly Defined)     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Science - Department of Chemistry (Rendy Gregory Kartika (00007612))     Work Location: 0331 A.R. Choppin Hall - Chemistry     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Department of Chemistry at Louisiana State University (LSU) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in Computational Chemistry (broadly defined). The successful candidate is expected to establish a nationally recognized and well-funded research program in computational chemistry, with particular emphasis on AI-enabled mesoscale modeling or AI-enabled chemical discovery, broadly defined. The successful candidate will develop and maintain an innovative and independent research program, demonstrate excellence in teaching and mentoring at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and contribute to service activities that advance the Department and the broader scientific community.   The candidate will join a dynamic and collaborative research environment with opportunities to build interdisciplinary partnerships within the Department of Chemistry, the Center for Computation and Technology, and across Louisiana State University. Participation in collaborative research initiatives, including large-scale grant proposals and industrial partnerships, is encouraged. The candidate will contribute to a collegial, supportive, and welcoming academic environment. This position is a joint appointment with the Center for Computation and Technology (CCT). Job Responsibilities   Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in chemistry based on departmental needs, such as courses in general chemistry, physical chemistry, and more advanced topics, and participate in departmental, university, and professional service activities. (50%) Establish and maintain a nationally recognized research program; secure external funding to support research activities; disseminate research findings through publications, presentations, and other appropriate venues; and mentor graduate and undergraduate research students. (50%)   Minimum Qualifications   Ph.D. in Chemistry or a related field. Demonstrated research expertise in AI-enabled computational chemistry, broadly defined.   Preferred Qualifications   Demonstrated commitment to excellence in research, teaching, and mentoring. Research expertise in AI-enabled mesoscale modeling or AI-enabled chemical discovery, broadly defined. Ability to work collaboratively, leverage institutional strengths, and contribute to research priorities aligned with the LSU Strategic Plan and Scholarship First Agenda. Additional Job Description Safety and Security Sensitive Job - Safety and security-sensitive positions are defined as those positions where any form of substance abuse may affect University activities through unsafe work behavior/performance or error in judgment; or where substance abuse could jeopardize the safety and well-being of employees, other personnel, or the public, or cause significant damage to university property. This includes positions requiring firearms, access to controlled substances, handling hazardous material, operating heavy equipment or machinery, etc. These positions are subject to drug screens per PS-67/FASOP HR-04. FERPA - As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality. Job Competencies Advanced proficiency in research and scholarship, teaching and mentorship, scientific innovation, collaboration and communication and professionalism.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Applicants should submit the application materials as a single PDF file, in the order listed below. Applications should consist of a cover letter, curriculum vitae, summary of research accomplishments (2 pages), description of future research plans (5 pages), and narrative of teaching philosophy (1 page). Copies of transcripts may be attached to the application; however, original transcripts will be required prior to an appointment. If the degree was received outside of the US, a credential evaluation will be required. Applicants should arrange to have a minimum of three letters of recommendation emailed directly to Senior HR Specialist, Mrs. Amy Commander (acom@lsu.edu). Please use the following subject line: LSU Computational Chemistry Faculty Search. Review of applications will begin October 30, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For questions regarding this position, please contact the Chair of the Faculty Search Committee, Prof. Revati Kumar, at revatik@lsu.edu. This position is considered a research or research-related support position and must undergo screenings per RS 17:1826.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 9, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): March 9, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/0229-Charles-E-Coates-Hall/Assistant-Professor---Performance-Studies-and-Screen-Arts_R00121357": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Performance Studies and Screen Arts",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor - Performance Studies and Screen Arts     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM HSS - Communication Studies (Bryan McCann (00007537))     Work Location: 0229 Charles E. Coates Hall     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Department of Communication Studies, in a joint appointment with the Screen Arts (SCRN) program, seeks a scholar-practitioner for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position (75% Communication Studies, 25% Screen Arts) beginning August 2027. We are looking for an innovative theorist and maker to conduct high-quality research—both written and produced—teach undergraduate and graduate courses, and actively mentor students in hands-on creative production. As our programs are dedicated to the ongoing evolution of intermedial practice, we seek candidates who will serve as a creative bridge between our experimental live performance laboratory, the HopKins Black Box theatre, and SCRN’s production environments (which encompass practical filmmaking, immersive media, and virtual production). The successful candidate will view practical production—in live stage performance, as well as film and television, live scenography, production design, or indie media—as a primary methodology and way of knowing. We strongly encourage applications from scholars whose backgrounds bridge Theatre, Film/Media Production, and Interdisciplinary Arts, provided they are committed to utilizing their hands-on production experience to drive rigorous academic publication and create original performances in the HopKins Black Box theatre and SCRN spaces. Required Qualifications ·         A Ph.D. or MFA in Performance Studies, Screen Arts, Media Production, Film, Theatre, or a closely related discipline (by the time of appointment). ·         A demonstrated, active agenda of \"practice-as-research\" or \"research-creation\" that balances hands-on media or theatrical production with academic publishing. ·         Research and creative credentials commensurate with a Comprehensive Doctoral University. ·         Evidence of excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications We seek a scholar-practitioner with a strong publication and practical production record (or clear potential) whose work complements existing faculty strengths. The ideal candidate will have practical experience in combining media creation with live performance or physical environments with a deep commitment to translating those skills into a laboratory setting. The candidate should have a strong interest in emerging and immersive media, while also being able to teach traditional performance studies and media production courses.  We are looking for a candidate who will actively involve and mentor students in original, devised, or experimental production making across both stage and screen. Areas of topical interest are open, but we especially welcome candidates whose work bridges physical stagecraft and scripting with digital/cinematic media, which may include: ·         Intermedial, multimedia, and devised performance ·         Translation of performance and directing techniques between live/staged and camera/media environments ·         Indie media creation, applied production, and public-facing storytelling ·         Scenography, production design, and physical world-building for stage and screen ·         Practical integration of live bodies with extended reality or virtual production spaces Salary Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Background Check An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Application Timeline Application review will begin November 12, 2026. Benefits LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more. THE LSU SYSTEM IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Before uploading, applicants should assemble all documents into one PDF file in the following order: 1. Cover Letter: Addressing your experience and dedication to written research, hands-on creative practice, teaching, and service. 2. Curriculum Vitae. 3. Description of Research Program: (Limit to 2 pages). Please explicitly address how you envision bridging and utilizing the HopKins Black Box theatre and SCRN’s production facilities for your research and creative works. 4. Sample of Scholarly Writing. 5. Portfolio of Creative Scholarship: Evidence of hands-on arts-based research, production design, media creation, or theatrical practice (e.g., links to video samples, prompt books, production photos, or portfolios). 6. Evidence of Teaching Excellence: (Limit to 2 pages). 7. References: A list of the names, titles, addresses, and contact information for three references who may be asked to provide letters of recommendation after the initial review. 8. Job Specification: The Department of Communication Studies is hiring for two assistant professors of performance studies this year; this position is 75% housed in Communication Studies, 25% housed in Screen Arts. Any candidates wishing to be considered for both positions must apply to each position independently and should indicate in writing that they are willing to be considered for both positions. Applicants may also attach copies of transcripts to their applications; original transcripts are required prior to hire. Please contact the chair of the search committee, Dr. Travis Brisini (tbrisini@lsu.edu) with questions regarding the status of your application or salary ranges.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 8, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): April 6, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/E0235-Howe-Russell-Kniffen-East-Geoscience-Complex/Assistant-Professor_R00121268": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Science - Department of Geology and Geophysics (Samuel J Bentley Sr. (00012115))     Work Location: E0235 Howe Russell Kniffen East Geoscience Complex     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Department of Geology and Geophysics at Louisiana State University invites applications for a tenure-track Hydrogeophysicist at the level of Assistant Professor. We seek either a geophysicist who works on water-related topics or a hydrogeologist who uses geophysical methods. The research focus area may include a broad range of earth and/or planetary settings. Collaborative opportunities at LSU include the College of Science, College of Engineering, College of Coast and the Environment, and the Energy Institute. LSU’s Center for Computation and Technology offers powerful platforms for research with a substantial computational component. Successful candidates will be expected to establish and maintain a vigorous, independent extramurally funded research program and to contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in the area of their expertise. Duties Include: 45% Establish and maintain a vigorous, independent extramurally funded research program. 45% Contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in the area of Geology and Geophysics. 10% Contribute to service to the Department of Geology and Geophysics and College of Science. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should have a Ph.D. in Hydrology, Hydrogeology, Geophysics, Earth Science, or related field at the time of appointment. Minimum Qualifications: Specific Experience Topic of the work is in some area of Hydrogeophysics, with demonstrated expertise in at least one area of Hydrology, Hydrogeology, or Geophysics. Postdoctoral experience and a record of successful independent research is preferred. This position may be asked to work during an official closure, but who is otherwise not required to report to the physical campus during a closure and whose absence does not present a risk to the safety, resources, and well-being of the campus per FASOP HR-01.      Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Applicants should submit their cover letter, Curriculum Vitae, statements of research and teaching interests, and three references who can provide letters of recommendation at a future date. An official copy of your transcript with the highest degree will be needed upon hire. For additional questions, please contact geology@lsu.edu or Lori Bond at lbond3@lsu.edu     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 7, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 31, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/E0314-Howe-Russell-Kniffen-East-Geoscience-Complex/McCord-Endowed-Chair-in-Geology-and-Geophysics_R00121265": {
      "title": "McCord Endowed Chair in Geology and Geophysics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: McCord Endowed Chair in Geology and Geophysics     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Science - Department of Geology and Geophysics (Samuel J Bentley Sr. (00012115))     Work Location: E0314 Howe Russell Kniffen East Geoscience Complex     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Department of Geology and Geophysics at Louisiana State University seeks an internationally renowned individual to fill the Charles T. McCord Chair in Geology at the rank of Full Professor or senior Associate. This position is fully endowed with dedicated annual research funding. We seek a distinguished geoscientist in the broad areas of critical minerals energy transition and related systems. Areas of expertise may include, but are not limited to, mineral resources, their genesis, formation, distribution, and characterization. Related subsurface systems may include energy, hydrothermal and fluid-mineral interactions in Earth and Planetary settings. Field and industrial components are welcome. The successful candidate will represent their field within the LSU Geology and Geophysics department and externally, while contributing to existing and expanding research collaborations. This role includes maintaining a world-class, externally funded research program that elevates the national and international profile of the department and university. Established leadership of interdisciplinary research teams is highly desirable.  The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in their area of expertise. LSU offers extensive areas for collaboration in critical minerals and materials, energy, engineering, chemistry, physics, environmental science, coastal research, and the newly formed LSU Energy Institute. Analytical facilities available at LSU include an electron microprobe, SEM-EDS/EBSD, XRD, LA-ICP-MS, Raman, XPS, TEM/STEM, micro-CT, clean-lab geochemistry, the LSU Light Source (synchrotron), and high-performance computing for research, including atomistic and thermodynamic modeling. LSU is a Carnegie R1 research university and a Land-, Sea-, and Space-Grant institution. The Department of Geology and Geophysics offers B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degrees and includes faculty with broad expertise across the field, experimental, analytical, computational, and theoretical geosciences. The Department has a strong record of research and graduate training, federal and industry-funded research, and an active and supportive alumni network. Duties Include: 45% Represent their field within the LSU Geology and Geophysics department and externally, while contributing to existing and expanding research collaborations. This role includes maintaining a world-class, externally funded research program that elevates the national and international profile of the department and university. 45% Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Geology and Geophysics and mentor undergraduate and graduate students. 10% Contribute professional, departmental, college, and university service and provide leadership appropriate to the holder of an endowed chair. Minimum Qualifications: PhD  in Geoscience or a closely related field, a distinguished record of high-impact research, scholarly distinction, and a portfolio of consistent external funding. A record of nationally and/or internationally distinguished research and scholarship; demonstrated success in research, publication, graduate mentoring, and external funding appropriate to appointment at the senior Associate Professor or Professor level. Preferred Qualifications: PhD  in Geoscience or a closely related field with 10 years experience and a substantial record of scientific leadership and high-impact scholarship in areas related to critical minerals; demonstrated ability to develop collaborative scientific research programs; sustained success in obtaining external research support; and excellence in graduate education and mentoring.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research interests and plans, statement of teaching and mentoring plans, and the names and contact information of five references who may be asked to provide letters of recommendation at a later stage. If confidentiality is to be maintained, please inform the Search Chair. Questions about the position may be directed to Jonathan E. Snow, Chair, McCord Search Committee at jesnow@lsu.edu or Lori Bond, Sr. Human Resources Specialist at lbond3@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 6, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 31, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
