    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/0202-Life-Sciences-Building/Dr-Shirley-C-Tucker-Chair-in-Lichenology_R00121175": {
      "title": "Dr. Shirley C. Tucker Chair in Lichenology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Dr. Shirley C. Tucker Chair in Lichenology     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Science - Department of Biological Sciences (Patrick Joseph DiMario (00009021))     Work Location: 0202 Life Sciences Building     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Department of Biological Sciences at Louisiana State University seeks an outstanding senior scholar at the rank of Associate or Full Professor to fill a tenured appointment as the Dr. Shirley C. Tucker Chair in Lichenology. The successful candidate will be engaged in scholarly research on the evolutionary biology of lichens, with an emphasis on collections-based research. Candidates should have internationally recognized scientific reputations and are expected to maintain a high-level, externally funded research program, and provide leadership both on campus and beyond. The Tucker Chair includes a competitive salary and access to discretionary funds generated by the endowment. LSU is designated a Carnegie Research I University and is one of a handful of distinguished universities to enjoy Land, Sea, and Space Grant status. The Department of Biological Sciences currently consists of 65 tenure-track faculty members studying a wide range of biological questions at scales from molecules to ecosystems. The candidate will build on LSU’s strengths in evolutionary biology, systematics, and collections-based research. Among the departmental resources is the Shirley C. Tucker Herbarium (https://www.lsu.edu/herbarium/), which is one of the largest herbaria in the Gulf South, home to ca. 400k specimens, including a nationally important collection of lichens. The Department offers B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degrees and has a strong record of success in research and student training. (See https://www.lsu.edu/science/biosci/ for more information.) Opportunities for a broad range of research interactions are available within the department, at the Museum of Natural Science, and throughout the University. Duties include: 50% - Lead a research team and maintain a vigorous, independent, and extramurally funded research program on the evolutionary biology of lichens; supervise graduate student research; and publish in highly ranked journals. 50% - Teach undergraduate and graduate courses and mentor graduate student research. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Biological Sciences, Botany, or a related field, and a demonstrated record of high-impact published research in lichenology. Advanced level of the following job competencies are required: Research on the evolutionary biology of lichens (collections-based); Securing and maintaining extramural research funding; Publishing in highly ranked journals; Undergraduate and graduate teaching; Graduate student mentoring and supervision; and Scientific leadership on campus and beyond. Preferred Qualifications Tenured or tenured-equivalent applicants with a strong record of past external funding are strongly preferred.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please upload a single pdf document containing the following elements in the order below. • Cover letter (2 pages or fewer) • Curriculum Vitae • Statement of research interests (4 pages or fewer) • Statement of teaching and mentoring interests (2 pages or fewer) • The names and contact information of three references who can provide letters of recommendation at a future date. An official transcript of your highest degree will be needed by date of hire. Review of applications will begin January 2027 and will continue until a candidate is selected. Questions about the position can be directed to the search committee chair, Laura Lagomarsino (llagomarsino1@lsu.edu) and/or senior HR specialist Lori Bond(lbond3@lsu.edu).     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 2, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 31, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/0202-Life-Sciences-Building/Assistant-Professor-Behavioral-Ecology_R00121160": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Behavioral Ecology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor-Behavioral Ecology     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Science - Department of Biological Sciences (Patrick Joseph DiMario (00009021))     Work Location: 0202 Life Sciences Building     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Department of Biological Sciences at Louisiana State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position. The Department houses >60 faculty spanning a range of disciplines, with strengths in ecology, evolutionary biology, neuroscience, and systematics. We seek a behavioral ecologist with a strong research program to run an independent and externally funded research program; teach undergraduate and graduate courses; and contribute to service to the department, university, and to the field. Duties include: ●       50% - Research: Develop and maintain a vigorous, independent, and extramurally funded research program. Participation in service activities related to research is expected. ●       50% - Teaching: Teaching assignments will be aligned with the candidate’s area of specialty at the graduate level and an introductory biology course at the undergraduate level. The candidate will mentor undergraduate and graduate students. Participation in service activities related to teaching and mentoring is expected. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent degree in biological sciences, ecology or related field; a successful record of independent research; and a strong background in behavioral ecology, animal behavior, or related discipline. Preferred Qualifications Postdoctoral research experience in behavioral ecology is preferred. Candidates whose research aligns with the LSU Scholarship First Agenda (https://www.lsu.edu/scholarship-first/) priorities of agriculture, biomedicine, coast, defense, and/or energy are particularly encouraged to apply. Candidates should demonstrate evidence of excellence in research and have identified potential extramural funding sources. Candidates are desired who demonstrate potential and/or evidence of excellence in mentoring and teaching students at both the undergraduate and graduate levels.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please upload a single pdf document containing the following elements in the order below. ● Cover letter (1 page max) ● CV (4 pages max) ● Research statement (2 pages max) ● Teaching statement (2 pages max) ● Contact information for three references, who may be contacted at a later date. For questions about the position, please contact Search Committee Chair Nick Mason (mason@lsu.edu) or Senior Human Resource Specialist Lori Bond (lbond3@lsu.edu).     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 2, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): November 15, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/2800-BEC-North-Undergrad-Pavilion/Instructor---Assistant-Director-of-CIA---CRM_R00121159": {
      "title": "Instructor - Assistant Director of CIA / CRM",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Instructor - Assistant Director of CIA / CRM     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM COB - School of Accounting (Dana Hollie (00008223))     Work Location: 2800 BEC North Undergrad Pavilion     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: JOB SUMMARY: The instructor will teach undergraduate / graduate level courses in the Department of Accounting. A graduate level class my be considered if applicant has expertise in a specialized field. A typical teaching load is 4 courses in the Fall and 4 courses in the Spring. Full time instructor will work with the Director of the Center for Internal Audit /Cybersecurity Risk Management to observe, learn and implement best practices for the students within the CIA /CRM program and develop key relationships with industry partners. JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: 65% - Teach Undergraduate / Graduate Classes in Accounting and / or Internal Auditing 25% - Serve as the Assistant Director of the Center for Internal Audit / Cybersecurity Risk Management which will include working closely with the CIA/CRM Director & Associate Director in carrying out the major functions of the program (e.g., student recruitment, placement, employer engagement, etc.). 10% - Assist with Internship Program Coordination: Support and coordinate the CIA's internship program, including working with students, faculty, employers, and College resources to facilitate internship opportunities and related academic requirements. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Education Level: PhD. in Accounting or business related discipline Degree Substitute: Master's degree in Accounting or Master's degree in a closely related business field with the Certified Internal Auditor certification, CISA, CISSP, CISM or CPA with 5+ years of experience PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Education Level: PhD in Accounting or closely related business related field Specific Experience : Industry related experience. Specific work experience with internal controls desired. Preferred Certifications / Licenses : CIA     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: For questions regarding this position or associated salary range, please contact Dr. Dana Hollie at danahollie1@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 2, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): March 31, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
