    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/W0227-Howe-Russell-Kniffen-West-Geoscience-Complex/Assistant-Professor---Human-Geography_R00120635": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Human Geography",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Human Geography     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM HSS - School of Geography and Anthropology (Jill C Trepanier (00002085))     Work Location: W0227 Howe Russell Kniffen West Geoscience Complex     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Department of Geography and Anthropology at Louisiana State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Human Geography specializing in Geographic Information Science and Technology (GISc&T) and geospatial data science. We seek a scholar with strong expertise in GISc&T and advanced geospatial methods to answer complex societal and human-environment questions. Relevant methodological expertise may include spatial-temporal analysis, geospatial data science, remote sensing, GeoAI, WebGIS, geovisualization, or related computational approaches. Candidates are not expected to specialize in all these areas. We are particularly interested in candidates who can expand the department's methodological capacity and contribute to innovative applications of geospatial technologies in research and teaching. The substantive area of specialization is open, but the successful candidate's scholarship must have a strong human-geographic dimension . Research areas may include, but are not limited to, health and well-being, population and inequality, food systems, energy and infrastructure, environmental change, hazards and disaster vulnerability, community resilience, critical GIS, or other societally relevant dimensions of human-environment interaction. We welcome scholarship that uses geospatial methods not simply as technical tools, but to advance understanding of important social, spatial, and environmental problems. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate instruction in GISc&T, spatial-temporal analysis, and environmental studies , while developing courses in their areas of methodological and topical expertise. The position will also offer opportunities to contribute to and collaborate with the department's Environmental Studies and Disaster Science and Management areas and to strengthen interdisciplinary geospatial training across departmental programs in both geography and anthropology. The successful candidate will be expected to develop an externally fundable research program; teach undergraduate and graduate courses; mentor undergraduate, master's, and doctoral students; and contribute to the department's growing emphasis on interdisciplinary and community-engaged scholarship. Opportunities exist for collaboration across geography and anthropology and with programs and units throughout LSU, such as the South Central Climate Adaptation Science Center. Job Description: 50% - Teach graduate or undergraduate courses and hold regular office hours.  Supervise graduate assistant(s) if assigned. 50% - Maintain an active research agenda with regular publications. Minimum Qualifications: Assistant Professor: PhD in Geography or related field or Anticipated Completion of Degree by August of 2027 Associate Professor: PhD in Geography or related field + 6 years of higher education experience Full Professor: PhD in Geography or related field + 10 years of higher education experience Proven record of excellence in teaching and scholarship.      Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Special Instructions: Applicants must provide: (1) a cover letter; (2) a current CV; (3) a research statement; (4) a teaching and mentoring statement (including teaching evaluations if available); and (5) the names and contact information of three references. Please attach all documents under the “Resume/CV” section of your application. Attachments are limited to five. To be considered, applicants should send their materials before October 15, 2026. The search will continue until the position is filled. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Jill Trepanier at jtrepa3@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 18, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): March 14, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): N     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/Music--Dramatic-Arts-Building/Assistant-Professor-of-Clarinet_R00120680": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clarinet",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Clarinet     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM CMDA - School of Music (James L Byo (00010414))     Work Location: Music & Dramatic Arts Building     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Louisiana State University School of Music invites applications for a tenure-track position, Assistant Professor of Clarinet, with appointment to begin in fall 2027. We seek artist-performers and teachers with demonstrated ability to attract a large studio of students who value learning in an engaged, collaborative, and vibrant School culture. Job Responsibilities: Teach applied clarinet at all levels and in all degree programs; teach woodwind specific courses, coach chamber music; advise graduate students, recruit promising student musicians; 40% Build and maintain a national and international research and creative activity profile as performer and teacher; participate with the woodwind faculty in chamber music; and contribute broadly to the artistic and educational milieu of a major School of Music at a Research I, flagship university. 40% Provide service and participate in faculty governance. Other duties as assigned. 20% Minimum Qualifications: Education Level: A doctorate in clarinet performance Degree Substitute: A doctorate in clarinet performance or equivalent professional experience Specific Experience: Distinguished record as an active performer; demonstrated excellence in and commitment to teaching a broad range of students with skill sets; and commitment to contributing broadly to the culture of the School of Music. Preferred Qualifications: Specific Experience: An additional area of expertise that extends one’s influence; evidence of dispositions that foster relationship-building, creative problem-solving, and innovative opportunities. LSU’s College of Music and Dramatic Arts is a performing arts community that trains, cultivates, prepares, and rewards excellent artists, educators, scholars, and performers, fostering passion for the arts, collaboration, and the creation of new works. We engage with our community, heightening our collective ability to communicate with expressive power and purpose. Louisiana State University and Agricultural and Mechanical College is a national flagship institution with world-class intellectual and creative resources. Located in a dynamic city situated on the Mississippi River, Baton Rouge represents the best of Louisiana's vibrant and evocative culture. The state capital, Baton Rouge is a thriving city that is home to both LSU and Southern University and numerous businesses and industrial facilities, with a metropolitan area population of over 700,000. The LSU School of Music offers a comprehensive music program with nearly 500 majors. It has over 50 faculty, 10 professional staff, and 75 graduate assistants. It sponsors nearly 300 recitals, concerts, operas, and lectures each academic year. Degrees offered include the Ph.D. (with concentrations in composition, experimental music and digital media, music education, musicology, and music theory), DMA (concentrations in music performance and choral, orchestral, and wind conducting,), MM, BM, BME, and BA (Liberal Arts). LSU has a vibrant and collaborative media arts community. The Center for Computation & Technology (CCT) supports LSU’s Cultural Computing Focus area, and includes Experimental Music & Digital Media, Digital Media Arts & Engineering, and Digital Arts, offering opportunities to compose for video games, digital animations, and film.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Review of applications begins October 19, 2026. To receive full consideration, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, contact information for three references, teaching philosophy (one page), and a document with links to recordings of live performances within the last three years on a platform such as SoundCloud or YouTube (preferably demonstrating both solo and chamber music performance). Teaching videos may be requested at a later date. Official transcripts are required prior to hire. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Susannah Knoll, Executive Assistant to the Dean/HR Analyst at cmdadeansoffice@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 16, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): March 15, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/0136-TW-Atkinson-Hall/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Architecture_R00120629": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Architecture",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Architecture     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM AD - School of Architecture (Marwan Ghandour (00048308))     Work Location: 0136 T.W. Atkinson Hall     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The LSU School of Architecture seeks applicants for a full-time, nine-month, at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor with expertise in advanced architectural design. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of design practice, teaching, and/or research in building and architectural design. The candidate is expected to teach graduate and undergraduate design studios and lecture/seminar courses in their area of expertise. The candidate will have the opportunity to collaborate with colleagues within LSU in general and the College of Art and Design in particular through research, teaching, program development, and governance. Minimum Qualifications Applicants should provide evidence of, or the potential for, teaching effectiveness, scholarship, innovative practice, communications skills, and collegiality. Minimum degree qualification is a Master of Architecture degree, or an equivalent degree in architecture or a closely related field. Context The LSU School of Architecture offers two professional, nationally accredited, degrees, the B Arch and M Arch, as well as a graduate research degree in Architecture, MS in Arch. Architecture faculty also participate in interdisciplinary college wide degrees: Doctor of Design in Cultural Preservation and the BA in Art and Design.  The College of Art & Design is a vibrant interdisciplinary unit composed of schools of Art, Architecture, Interior Design, and Landscape Architecture. The LSU Coastal Ecosystem Design Studio (CEDS) and the Fabrication Lab add a growing multidisciplinary dimension to our degree programs. LSU is dedicated to the development of a collaborative, globally engaged learning environment that prioritizes innovative, effective, and culturally creative practices and leadership skills. LSU is located in Baton Rouge, the capital of Louisiana. Along with the cities of New Orleans and Lafayette nearby, South Louisiana is home to great historical traditions and populations, known internationally for its music, food, native architecture and dynamic natural environment. As an institution, LSU is the Flagship University of the State and leads the nation in knowledge and research of coastal environments.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Applications should include the following materials: 1. Letter of interest with a narrative description of applicant’s background, scholarly interests and qualifications for the position (max 1500 words). The narrative should include research/creative practice statement and teaching statement. 2. Detailed curriculum vitae with contact information 3. Names of at least three references with contact information 4. Portfolio of scholarly, teaching and creative work (maximum 50 MB) Application materials are to be submitted to the university’s online application portal. Original transcripts will be required prior to hire. Although the positions will remain open until filled, for best consideration, candidates should submit their materials by January 12, 2027. All submissions will remain confidential until selection for on-campus interviews. For more information, please contact the School of Architecture archsearch@lsu.edu. For more information about LSU, see www.lsu.edu; for information about the College, see https://design.lsu.edu; for information about the School, see https://design.lsu.edu/architecture/     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 15, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): March 14, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/0210J-OK-Allen-Hall/Assistant-Professor----18th-Century-British-Literature_R00120555": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor  - 18th-Century British Literature",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor - 18th-Century British Literature     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM HSS - Department of English (Susan D Weinstein (00005145))     Work Location: 0210J O.K. Allen Hall     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Department of English at Louisiana State University (LSU) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of British literature and culture of the Long 18th Century (1660-1830) , beginning in August of 2027.   Located in Baton Rouge, LSU is the flagship land-grant, sea-grant, and space-grant institution in Louisiana and a Research 1 (R1) University. We support research and teaching in a broad range of fields and many interdisciplinary programs.   Requirements: Ph.D., with expertise in B ritish literature and culture of the Long 18th Century (1660-1830), by the time the position begins (August 2027); record of publication or strong promise of future scholarly achievement. Preference given to candidates who can teach and direct undergraduate and graduate research on literature of the entire period.   Teaching Expectations: The teaching load is 2/2 and includes graduate and undergraduate courses in Long 18th-Century British literature and culture. The new hire in this position is expected to teach undergraduate courses in the annual rotations of English 3020 (British Literature I: The Middle Ages, Renaissance, and 18th Century) and English 3022 (British Literature II: Romantics, Victorians, and Moderns) and to serve on graduate dissertation committees. They will also have the opportunity to design new courses and work with existing interdisciplinary programs and collaborations.   Research Expectations: Competitive candidates should maintain an active scholarly profile on par with the expectations of a Research 1 Institution. The College provides support for research and faculty development.   Application Deadline: The deadline for all application materials is November 2, 2026. Please note that an offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check.    LSU IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER.       Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Application Materials: 1. Letter of application (2 pages) 2. Current CV 3. 2-3 page dissertation abstract or research statement 4. Names (with contact information) of three references from whom we may request confidential letters of recommendation. Please attach all documents under the “Resume/CV” section of your application. Attachments are limited to five. Writing samples may be requested at a later point. First-round interviews will be conducted via Zoom in mid-December or early January. Questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges may be addressed to the English Department administrator, Mr. Richard Landry, at rland26@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 14, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): March 13, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/2300-BEC-South-Grad-Pavilion/Assistant-Professor_R00120502-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM COB - School of Economics (Faik A Koray (00006987))     Work Location: 2300 BEC South Grad Pavilion     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: JOB SUMMARY: The Department of Economics invites applications for a tenure-track position in applied microeconomics at the Assistant Professor rank to begin in Fall 2027. Applicants should have strong research skills and expertise in one of the fields listed: Microeconomics, Public Economies, Health, Education and Welfare, Labor and Demographic Economics, Law and Economics, Industrial Economics, Energy, and Environmental Economics. Applicants should submit a cover letter, CV, job market paper, copies of selected research papers, and graduate transcripts. Applicants should also arrange for three recommendation letters to be submitted. JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: 50% - Engaging in academic research and publishing in academic journals 40% - Teaching senior level / graduate courses in Applied Microeconomics 10% - Serving on department, college, and university committees MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Education Level - - PhD in Economics or related field; ABD candidates will be considered but they should receive their Ph.D. by August 2027. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Education Level - - PhD in Economics or related field Years of Experience: 0-10 Specific Experience: Demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching or demonstrated potential for excellence JOB COMPETENCIES: Research - Advanced Course Instruction - Advanced Communication - Advanced     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: For questions about this position or the associated salary range, please contact Dr. Faik Koray at eokora@lsu.edu This position is considered research-related and an RS:17 screening is required.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 11, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): March 10, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
