    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/0232-AR-Choppin-Hall---Chemistry/Assistant--Associate-or-Full-Professor-in-Analytical-Chemistry_R00120454": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor in Analytical Chemistry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant, Associate or Full Professor in Analytical Chemistry     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Science - Department of Chemistry (Rendy Gregory Kartika (00007612))     Work Location: 0232 A.R. Choppin Hall - Chemistry     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Department of Chemistry at Louisiana State University (LSU) invites applications for an open-rank faculty position in Analytical Chemistry at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor.   The successful candidate is expected to establish a nationally recognized and well-funded research program in any area of chemistry, with emphasis on measurement or instrumental science, broadly defined. Candidates with research expertise that can contribute to forensic chemistry are particularly encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will develop and maintain an innovative and independent research program, demonstrate excellence in teaching and mentoring at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and contribute to service activities that advance the Department and the broader scientific community.   The candidate will join a dynamic and collaborative research environment with opportunities to build interdisciplinary partnerships within the Department of Chemistry and across Louisiana State University. Participation in collaborative research initiatives, including large-scale grant proposals and industrial partnerships, is encouraged. The candidate will contribute to a collegial, supportive, and welcoming academic environment. Job Responsibilities   Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in chemistry based on departmental needs, such as courses in general chemistry, analytical chemistry, forensic chemistry, and more advanced topics, and participate in departmental, university, and professional service activities. (50%) Establish and maintain a nationally recognized research program; secure external funding to support research activities; disseminate research findings through publications, presentations, and other appropriate venues; and mentor graduate and undergraduate research students. (50%)   Assistant Professor Rank Minimum Qualifications   Ph.D. in Chemistry or a related field. Demonstrated research expertise in measurement or instrumental science, broadly defined.   Preferred Qualifications   Demonstrated commitment to excellence in research, teaching, and mentoring. Research expertise that can contribute to forensic chemistry in areas including but not limited to trace analysis, development of field-ready tools, chemometrics, automated data interpretation, and development of new analytical methods and sensors. Ability to work collaboratively, leverage institutional strengths, and contribute to research priorities aligned with the LSU Strategic Plan and Scholarship First Agenda. Associate Professor Rank Minimum Qualifications   Ph.D. in Chemistry or a related field. Demonstrated research expertise in measurement or instrumental science, broadly defined. Minimum of 4 years of experience at the rank of Assistant Professor Current external research funding   Preferred Qualifications   Demonstrated commitment to excellence in research, teaching, and mentoring. Research expertise that can contribute to forensic chemistry in areas including but not limited to trace analysis, development of field-ready tools, chemometrics, automated data interpretation, and development of new analytical methods and sensors. Ability to work collaboratively, leverage institutional strengths, and contribute to research priorities aligned with the LSU Strategic Plan and Scholarship First Agenda. Professor Rank Minimum Qualifications   Ph.D. in Chemistry or a related field. Demonstrated research expertise in measurement or instrumental science, broadly defined. Currently at the rank of Associate Professor Current external research funding   Preferred Qualifications   Demonstrated commitment to excellence in research, teaching, and mentoring. Research expertise that can contribute to forensic chemistry in areas including but not limited to trace analysis, development of field-ready tools, chemometrics, automated data interpretation, and development of new analytical methods and sensors. Ability to work collaboratively, leverage institutional strengths, and contribute to research priorities aligned with the LSU Strategic Plan and Scholarship First Agenda. Additional Job Description Safety and Security Sensitive Job - Safety and security-sensitive positions are defined as those positions where any form of substance abuse may affect University activities through unsafe work behavior/performance or error in judgment; or where substance abuse could jeopardize the safety and well-being of employees, other personnel, or the public, or cause significant damage to university property. This includes positions requiring firearms, access to controlled substances, handling hazardous material, operating heavy equipment or machinery, etc. These positions are subject to drug screens per PS-67/FASOP HR-04. FERPA - As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality. This position is considered a research or research-related support position and must undergo screenings per RS 17:1826. Job Competencies Advanced proficiency in research and scholarship, teaching and mentorship, scientific innovation, collaboration and communication and professionalism.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Applicants should submit the application materials as a single PDF file, in the order listed below. Applications should consist of a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research portfolio, and narrative of teaching philosophy (1 page). Applicants seeking appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor should arrange to have a minimum of three letters of recommendation emailed directly to Senior HR Specialist Mrs. Amy Commander (acom@lsu.edu). Please use the following subject line: LSU Analytical Chemistry Faculty Search. The research portfolio should focus on future research directions. Applicants seeking appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor should provide the names and contact information of a minimum of three references. The research portfolio should describe previous, current, and future research directions. Copies of transcripts may be attached to the application; however, original transcripts will be required prior to an appointment. If the degree was received outside of the US, a credential evaluation will be required. Review of applications will begin October 30, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For questions regarding this position, please contact the Chair of the Faculty Search Committee, Prof. Noemie Elgrishi, at noemie@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 10, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): March 9, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/0225-Human-Ecology-Building/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor_R00120344": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant or Associate Professor     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM COA - Department of Textiles Apparel Design and Merchandising (Bruce Cameron (00054395))     Work Location: 0225 Human Ecology Building     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The LSU College of Agriculture is seeking to fill a tenure-track assistant/associate professor position in the Department of Textiles, Apparel Design, and Merchandising (TAM). 50% Teaching: teach undergraduate and graduate courses that may include but are not limited to Retail Mathematics, Retail Buying and Merchandise Management, Sustainability for Apparel and Textiles, Global Textile and Apparel Economics, Fashion Entrepreneurship, Advanced Topics in Fashion Merchandising, Consumer Behavior in the Apparel Merchandising Environment, Fashion, Luxury and Lifestyle brands, and Research Methods. The 50% teaching appointment will consist of a standard teaching load of 2 three-hour credit courses per semester in the fall and spring only 45% Research: Develop research in areas of Textiles, Apparel Design & Merchandising with an emphasis in innovations in merchandising technology, artificial intelligence integration, digital retailing/transformation, consumer behavior, and/or fashion branding. Develop an independent and collaborative research program related to their field, acquire external funding for scholarship with the expectation that they will disseminate their research findings. 5% Service: Contribute to advising and recruitment of both undergraduate and graduate students. Professional involvement in community; membership in appropriate professional and/or academic organizations; ability to develop industry partnerships. FERPA: -As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality. Additional Information: This position is considered a research or research-related support position and must undergo screenings per RS 17:1826. Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Textile, Apparel Design & Merchandising or related area. Established college-level teaching record as graduate student, instructor or above; demonstrated record of scholarship, participation in juried exhibitions, and ability to obtain external funding; evidence of teaching excellence, graduate and undergraduate level advising, and service consistent with appointment. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Textile, Apparel Design & Merchandising or related area with 3 years of service. Demonstrated ability to teach a variety of courses within the Textile, Apparel Design and Merchandising curriculum (e.g., Retail Mathematics, Retail Buying and Merchandise Management, Sustainability for Apparel and Textiles, Global Textile and Apparel Economics, Fashion Entrepreneurship, Advanced Topics in Fashion Merchandising, Consumer Behavior in the Apparel Merchandising Environment, Fashion, Luxury and Lifestyle brands, and Research Methods); industry experience; professional involvement in community; membership in appropriate professional and/or academic organizations; ability to develop industry partnerships. SALARY AND BENEFITS: Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The LSU has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances, university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. APPLICATION DEADLINE: Until a suitable candidate is identified.       Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please attach a cover letter with statement of professional interest and goals, resume, university transcripts, and the names and contact information for three professional references. Official transcript(s) are not required at time of application but are required at time of hire. A statement of research philosophy and teaching philosophy needs to be included as part of the application. Questions about the position (not application materials) should be emailed to: Dr. Chunmin Lang (cmlang@lsu.edu) Chair of the Search Committee     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 9, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): March 8, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/Campbell-B-Hodges-Hall/Professional-in-Residence--Public-Relations-_R00120174-1": {
      "title": "Professional-in-Residence (Public Relations)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Professional-in-Residence (Public Relations)     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Manship School of Mass Communication (Kim Bissell (00082011))     Work Location: Campbell B. Hodges Hall     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The LSU Manship School of Mass Communication invites applications for a nine-month, non-tenure track position as a Professional-In-Residence for the Public Relations area to begin in Spring 2027. We seek a distinguished communication practitioner to teach four courses per semester in the Manship School undergraduate core curriculum and/or courses in public relations, strategic communication, corporate communication, crisis communications and courses related to their areas of expertise. Job Responsibilities: Teach four undergraduate courses per semester in the Manship School of Mass Communication and develop a portfolio of service activities. The PIR may assist with supervision of undergraduate research and creative work in lieu of a fourth course. 100% Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in public relations, mass communication, or related field; 7 years of experience. Degree Substitute : Bachelor's degree in public relations, mass communication, or related field with professional work-related experience that clearly documents the qualifications to teach the course; 10 or more years of industry-related professional experience. Additional Requirements: FERPA -As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide cover letter, resume, (3) professional references and transcripts. Official transcripts, if needed are required prior to hire. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Dr. Chun Yang at cyang10@lsu.edu     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 4, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): October 31, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
