    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/0101-Life-Sciences-Building/Instructor_R00118737": {
      "title": "Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Instructor     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Science - BioS - Molecular Biology - Gene Expression (David Donze (00009160))     Work Location: 0101 Life Sciences Building     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: This individual will be responsible for development of a hybrid online/in person Introductory Biology laboratory course (BIOL 1212) and a completely online Human Physiology course (BIOL 2160) and teaching the BIOL 2160 course during the 2026/27 AY. After the 2026/27 AY, this individual will teach the online BIOL 2160 course and up to two Introductory Biology Program courses each semester or other courses as needed. This individual will provide service in support of the Introductory Biology Program or Department of Biological Sciences as needed. Duties: 50% Teach online BIOL 2160 during one term each semester and up to two Introductory Biology Program courses each semester. 35% Develop an online Human Physiology course (BIOL 2160) and a hybrid online/in person laboratory course (BIOL 1212) during the initial year of appointment. 10% Provide service in support of the Introductory Biology Program and Department of Biological Sciences as needed. This may include providing help with required program assessment each semester or developing additional online courses. 5% Additional duties as deemed necessary by the Associate Chair of Introductory Biology, Associate Chair of Undergraduate Studies, or the Department Chair to fit the changing needs of a growing department. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in Biological Sciences, Biochemistry, Microbiology or related field. Three years experience with standard laboratory techniques used in biology laboratories. Experience teaching at the college level. This can include experience as a graduate teaching assistant. Experience teaching online courses. Strong training in biology, experience with multimedia or other modern instructional technology or both; familiarity with practices of active learning and inquiry-based learning. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Biological Sciences, Biochemistry, Microbiology or related field with experience with standard laboratory techniques used in biology laboratories. Experience teaching at the college level. This can include experience as a graduate teaching assistant. Experience teaching online courses. Strong training in biology, experience with multimedia or other modern instructional technology or both; familiarity with practices of active learning and inquiry-based learning.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please submit a current cv and contact information of 3 references. An official transcript showing highest degree obtained will be needed prior to hire. For questions or concerns regarding the position, please contact Lori Bond at lbond3@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 14, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 11, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/French-House/Instructor---Part-Time_R00118297": {
      "title": "Instructor - Part-Time",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Instructor - Part-Time     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM AA - HC - Instruction (Drew Lamonica Arms (00003093))     Work Location: French House     Pay Grade:     Job Description: This part-time instructor will focus on teaching one introductory course worth three credit hours in the Ogden Honors College. Job Responsibilities Teach an introductory course worth three credit hours in the Ogden Honors College. (100%) Additional Information FERPA - As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health-related matter, they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students, or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. Experience teaching and/or developing introductory courses in Honors     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and three professional references, including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the Ogden Honors College at (225) 578-8831.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 11, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): February 7, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using